  "name": "Gyudon (Japanese Beef & Rice Bowls)",
  "servings": 4,
  "notes": [
    "US customary quantities. This fixed variant uses dashi, fried eggs, and the optional sesame garnish.",
    "Oil is allocated separately: 2 tablespoons for onions and 2 for eggs, following the article instructions.",
    "Beef starts already thinly sliced. Rice starts cooked and hot, as specified by the source ingredient list; rice cooking requires a separate graph.",
    "Additional soy sauce to taste is optional in the source and excluded from this fixed allocation. Stock substitutions are not separate branches.",
    "All precedence in this graph follows food-flow edges. No extra action dependsOn links are needed.",
    "Eggs, rice portioning, and scallion preparation can proceed independently of the beef branch. A scheduler should align their completion with final assembly.",
    "beef_skillet and beef_burner refer to the same physical resources throughout the beef branch; egg_skillet and egg_burner designate a separate pan and burner. A future scheduler must map and reserve them.",
    "Passive simmering does not require continuous hands-on work, but the cook must remain available to monitor it. The current schema cannot represent intermittent attention.",
    "Resource quantities such as four serving bowls and equipment occupancy between actions are not modeled by the current equipment list.",
    "Planned durations marked estimate are inferred, not source timings. Confirm the stated food condition before marking an action complete.",
    "Outputs represent all four servings collectively. Cleaning and equipment setup outside the described actions are not timed."
  ],
